START
    initialize the crypto library (stop if it fails)
    disable core dumps and debugger attachment
    install handlers: Ctrl+C, Ctrl+\, kill, terminal closed -> set stopRequested
    ignore Ctrl+Z (no suspend while the terminal hides typing)
    take the single-instance lock on vault.lock (stop if another instance holds it)
    verify the audit log hash chain
        IF the chain is broken:
            keep the old log as vault.audit.log.unverified-<time>
            start a new log with audit_log / integrity_failed
            show a warning
    log session_start
    sessionKey = empty, locked in RAM
    entries = empty
    vaultUnlocked = false
    userWantsToExit = false

    REPEAT until userWantsToExit, stopRequested or end of input:

        IF vault.json does not exist:
            show "1. Create vault" / "2. Exit"
            read menuChoice (at most 1 character)
            "1" -> CREATE VAULT
            "2" -> userWantsToExit = true
            other -> show "Please choose 1 or 2"

        ELSE IF vaultUnlocked is false:
            show "Vault is locked" / "1. Unlock vault" / "2. Exit"
            read menuChoice
            "1" -> UNLOCK VAULT
            "2" -> userWantsToExit = true
            other -> show "Please choose 1 or 2"

        ELSE:
            show "1. Add entry" / "2. View entries" / "3. Lock vault" /
                 "4. Exit" / "5. Reveal one password"
            read menuChoice
            "1" -> ADD ENTRY
            "2" -> VIEW ENTRIES
            "3" -> LOCK VAULT
            "4" -> userWantsToExit = true
            "5" -> REVEAL PASSWORD
            other -> show "Please choose 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5"

    wipe entries and sessionKey
    log session_end (success or interrupted)
    restore the terminal settings
    show "Program ended"


CREATE VAULT:
    identify the OS account (stop with access_denied if unknown)
    read a new master password without displaying it
    IF it is not 15-256 printable ASCII, or it is guessable
       (few distinct characters, a repeated block, a sequence such as
        12345 or qwerty, or a common word with a weak remainder):
        show the password rules, log validation_failed, return
    read it again without displaying it
    IF the two do not match:
        show "The passwords do not match", log confirmation_failed, return
    create a random salt
    derive the key with Argon2id (moderate cost) and wipe the master password
    encrypt "[]" with XChaCha20-Poly1305, a random nonce and
        the owner account as authenticated data
    write vault.json (version 3) as a new file, owner-only
    IF the write succeeds:
        create vault.attempts as "0 0 0"
        log vault_create success
    wipe the temporary key
    (the vault stays locked; the user unlocks it next)


UNLOCK VAULT:
    load vault.attempts
    IF it is missing while the vault exists:
        log counter_missing, start a lockout, show the wait time, return
    IF it is malformed or a symlink:
        show "The vault stays locked", log state_error, return
    IF a cooldown is running:
        show the remaining seconds, log rate_limited, return
    read the master password without displaying it
    record the attempt in vault.attempts BEFORE checking it
        (5th failure -> cooldown 60 s, doubling each lockout up to 1 hour)
    IF the password is empty, blank or too long:
        log validation_failed, return
    read and strictly parse vault.json
    check that the current account owns the vault
    derive the key from the password and the saved salt (wipe the password)
    decrypt and verify the authentication tag
    IF verification fails:
        wipe the key
        show "Incorrect password, or the vault file is damaged"
        log failure, return
    strictly parse every decrypted record (reject the whole vault on any error)
    reset vault.attempts
    keep the key and entries for this session
    vaultUnlocked = true, log vault_unlock success


ADD ENTRY:
    check that the current account is the vault owner
    read service (required, max 100 bytes)
    read website (optional, max 2048 bytes)
    read username (optional, max 256 bytes)
    read password without displaying it (required, 1-256 printable ASCII)
    read notes (optional, max 2048 bytes)
    IF any field is invalid (too long, control characters, blank when required):
        cancel the entry, log input_rejected / validation_failed, return
    add the entry and SAVE VAULT
    IF the save fails:
        remove the entry, show "It was not added", log save_failed
    ELSE:
        log entry_add success


VIEW ENTRIES:
    check that the current account is the vault owner
    show service, website, username and notes of each entry
    show each password as "[hidden]"
    log entry_view success


REVEAL PASSWORD:
    check that the current account is the vault owner
    require an interactive terminal for output
    read the entry number (digits only, in range)
    ask "Type yes" to confirm
    IF confirmed:
        log password_reveal success
        show that one password
    ELSE:
        show "Reveal cancelled"


SAVE VAULT:
    check that the current account is the vault owner
    serialize the entries into a wiped buffer
    encrypt with the session key, a NEW random nonce and the owner binding
    IF vault.json changed since unlock:
        show "The vault changed since unlock", log file_changed, fail
    write a new temporary file (owner-only) and rename it over vault.json


LOCK VAULT:
    wipe entries and sessionKey
    vaultUnlocked = false
    show "Vault locked", log vault_lock success
